  "conclusions": [
    "Stale action/resource statistics reproduce the observed action-time index scan with130 nonmatching rows filtered per candidate document.",
    "ANALYZE of the TEMP audit table alone switches the baseline query to the existing partial resource/time index, without changing aggregation semantics.",
    "ORDER BY resource first, OFFSET0 and singleton ANY did not fix the stale-statistics condition. OFFSET0 regressed to a sequential scan after statistics refresh.",
    "An additional full covering index was tested only after statistics refresh; the existing partial index remained selected. This does not justify a production index change."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "TEMP-table buffers are local hits, not the shared hits of the application plan. Compare plan shape and row work, not absolute buffer counts across those fixtures.",
    "Only the popularity subquery over candidate documents is timed; these are not full API or full FTS latencies.",
    "Shared host had concurrent tests/builds; timings are observations, not capacity guarantees.",
    "This distribution has130 reads concentrated on one document. It does not establish a universal PostgreSQL planner choice for all distributions.",
    "No automatic ANALYZE, global optimizer tuning, or service configuration mutation was added."
  ],
